# Cloudflare Pages rewrite rules — keep the URLs the site links as the URLs the host serves.
#
# Astro builds each route to <route>/index.html and, with trailingSlash: "never", every link in the
# HTML is slash-free (/menu). Pages' own asset resolution answers a slash-free path to a directory
# with a 308 to the slashed form, so the link in the nav bar and the address in the browser bar
# disagree with the canonical tag, which says /menu.
#
# A 200 rule is a rewrite, not a redirect: Pages evaluates _redirects before it resolves assets, so
# /menu is served from the file with no hop and no second URL. Nothing here redirects anything, so a
# rule cannot bounce into Pages' automatic trailing-slash 308 and back — the failure mode of a rule
# pair, which would be a loop the guest feels as a blank screen.
#
# scripts/verify-dist.mjs asserts this file exists, covers every non-root route, and that each
# destination is a real file in the build.
/menu /menu/index.html 200
/table /table/index.html 200
/visit /visit/index.html 200
